// The first thing a new player hears: Pr1nted hands them over to Mia.
//
// Runs on the MAIN MENU, before any map is loaded, so nothing here may refer
// to a country, a province or a turn -- there is no game yet.
//
// NOBODY SAYS "dials in". A speaker arriving on the link is the window's job
// -- changing speaker drops the signal and brings the new one up through the
// static -- so writing it as an action would put the stage direction on
// screen AND leave the effect undone. The end of the call is act=tune_out for
// the same reason.

:: anchor=left size=20 pad=26 enter=type speed=42 line=1.4

@Pr1nted
Hello, who is this?
---
@
...
---
@Pr1nted
Oh... You're new here... What? §**never ran a country before?**§
---
@
...
---
@Pr1nted
:: delay=1.1
... You know? My bad...
---
@Pr1nted
:: enter=type speed=42
However, I don't have enough to do the tutorial myself, so I'll have to leave
you with a friend of mine, ok? I need time, have to make future updates, right?
---
@Signals Officer
Hello? What §**Pr1nted**§?
---
@Pr1nted
Umm... Hey Mia, I need a /tiny little favour,/ could you help a new player around?
---
@Signals Officer
</Sigh/>
---
@Pr1nted
**Come 'on'!** What do I pay you for?
---
@Signals Officer
Fine... Alright, alright.
---
@Pr1nted
Good! So Miss Mia will show you around, how the game works and the basics of it,
or if you know the basics, but want to talk about specifics, tell us now,
> Show me the basics -> basics
> I know the basics, talk specifics -> specifics
---
@
{choice}
---
@Signals Officer
Great, let's get started.
---
@Pr1nted
:: act=tune_out
Great, hopefully you two get along! Pr1nted out.
